In `@src/utils/active-jobs-storage.js` around lines 29 - 30, Parsed storage may be
null/array/other non-object values so replace the direct JSON.parse(...) usage
with a normalized-map check: after const raw =
sessionStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY) do const parsed = raw ? JSON.parse(raw) :
undefined and then set const jobs = (parsed && typeof parsed === 'object' &&
!Array.isArray(parsed)) ? parsed : {}; apply the same normalization in every
other spot that currently does JSON.parse(raw) with a `{}` fallback (the other
occurrences around the same module that read STORAGE_KEY/sessionStorage.getItem,
e.g., the functions that restore or read active jobs) so callers (e.g.,
getActiveJobs) always receive a plain object map.
```

</details>

